              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Abnormalities vary in severity, onset, and progression; may be seen as Histologic examination of muscle—muscle early as 6 weeks; tend to stabilize by 6 months. fiber necrosis and regeneration; myofiber",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Stunting and ineffective suckling—may be mineralization (may be dramatic); myofiber",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "evident in younger pups.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cardiac failure— hypertrophy (may be variation in myofiber",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "may occur owing to cardiomyopathy.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Severe size); fibrosis.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "muscle contractures may develop.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Spinal reflexes—normal initially; may become hypoactive.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "subheading",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cats",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Dystrophin deficient—muscle hypertrophy;",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "None proven effective.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "stiff gait; cervical rigidity; exercise intolerance;",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "vomiting; may see calcified nodules on the",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "tongue.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Usually young animals but not",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "apparent in one cat until 21 months of age.",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Other hereditary myopathies in cats may",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "cause muscle atrophy; weakness; ventroflexion",
              "pdf_page": 1020,
              "printed_page": 938,
              "column": 2,
              "subheading": "Cats"
            }
          ]
